{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [Eb] | [Gm] [Eb] | [Bb] [Eb] | [Gm] [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb][Bb]A name [Eb]is written in the [Bb]scroll
A[Eb]mong the [F]sons of [Gm]Judah
The [Eb]record keeps the [F]family [Gm]whole
Though [Bb]few have heard his [F]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He is the [Eb]brother of the [Bb]wife
Of [Eb]Hodiah [F]known in [Gm]Judea
Her [Eb]sister stands with[F]in the [Gm]life
A thread of an[F]cient lineage
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Father of [Eb]Keilah the [Gm]Garmite
And [Bb]Eshte[Eb]moa the Maa[Gm]cathite
His [Eb]name is bound to [F]holy ground
[Gm]In the tribal [Eb]record found
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Keilah stands with [Eb]Akzib near
[Bb]And Mareshah in the list
Nine [Eb]towns with [F]their vil[Gm]lages ap[Eb]pear
[F]In the allot[Gm]ted land of [F]bliss
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Eshte[Bb]moa with its pastu[Eb]reland
[Bb]Where shepherds keep their flocks
[Eb]Part of the in[F]heritance [Gm]planned
For the sons of [F]Judah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Father [Eb]of Keilah [Gm]the Garmite
And [Bb]Eshte[Eb]moa the Maa[Gm]cathite
His [Eb]name is bound to [F]holy ground
[Gm]In the tribal [Eb]record found
